-- NorthstarIQ — Qualification drift: a Lead still holding a claim its current
-- business state no longer substantiates
--
-- ⚠️ LATER-CREATED REPRODUCIBILITY EVIDENCE — written 2026-09-01 AFTER the
-- controlled lifecycle validation. It was NOT used during that validation and
-- is not historical evidence. It exists so the drift pattern can be re-checked.
--
-- THE PATTERN. A Lead qualifies at MQL under the active policy, and the Flow
-- writes MQL_Basis__c naming the segment that qualified it. Later, a legitimate
-- correction to NumberOfEmployees re-segments the Lead. Status never changes, so
-- the preventive gate — which fires only on a Status change — never re-runs. The
-- recorded basis and the current segment now disagree.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS IS NOT A SALESFORCE DEFECT. Correcting a company's employee count is
-- ordinary, legitimate business data maintenance and must stay permitted. The
-- gate governs the moment of transition; nothing governs the record afterwards.
-- That gap is precisely why an independent detective control exists.
--
-- WHAT THIS QUERY IS AND IS NOT. It surfaces the RECORDS. It does not re-derive
-- the verdict: MQL eligibility is defined by Segment_Band__mdt.MQL_Eligible__c
-- and judged by NorthstarIQ's MQL Qualification Integrity control, which reads
-- the same governed configuration. Do not treat the segment names in the filter
-- as a second definition of eligibility — read the CMDT for that. They are here
-- only so the query is selective, and they must be revisited if the bands change.
--
-- Observed 2026-09-01 during the controlled run: NIQ Fixture 02 appeared here,
-- and NorthstarIQ independently reported it Failed — "segment is not one the
-- business qualifies". That is historical execution evidence, not a current count.
--
-- Read-only. Safe to run against any org.

SELECT Id,
       Name,
       Company,
       Status,
       NumberOfEmployees,
       Segment__c,
       Segment_Basis__c,
       MQL_Basis__c,
       Lifecycle_Stage_Entered__c
FROM Lead
WHERE Status = 'MQL'
  AND MQL_Basis__c != null
  AND Segment__c = 'SMB'
ORDER BY Lifecycle_Stage_Entered__c DESC
